name pair-cover-1
timeout 400

# THE COVER RIG: the one file in which the flight's cover rule can be SEEN firing, and it is a rig in
# the sense mig29-radar-notch is — a geometry built so that one mechanism is observable in isolation,
# not a task anybody would fly.
#
# THE RULE (doc/formation.md section 6): a member does not fire a round that would BIND it while a
# flight-mate is already bound, because a bound shooter is flying at its own antenna and a flight in
# which nobody is free cannot answer a launch. It holds at most as long as its own shot would bind it;
# after that two rounds in the air beat one.
#
# WHY IT NEEDS A RIG. The rule costs what the WEAPON costs, and on the AIM-120 that is almost nothing:
# [MESS, pair-2v2-asym] a head-on shot at Rtr goes active 0.3 s after launch, so the binding is three
# ticks long and two members practically never overlap. Two things are therefore set here, both taken
# from the existing tree rather than invented:
#   1. the EARLY-LAUNCH doctrine (`pilot_shot_rtr 1.4` / `pilot_lock_nm 20`, doc/duels.md section 3) —
#      a shot from 15+ nm has a time-to-active of 8.75 s instead of 0.3 s [MESS], so a binding exists
#      at all;
#   2. the two bandits are staggered 3 km in range, so the two members reach their own firing
#      parameters SEVERAL SECONDS apart instead of within the same second. That matters because the
#      "mate is bound" bit travels in the PPLI: a member that shot less than one net cycle ago is not
#      yet known to be bound, and the rule cannot act on what has not arrived. [MESS, the same file
#      without the stagger] both vipers fired 0.4 s apart, spent 7.9 s bound TOGETHER, and the rule
#      never fired once.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 (SUCCESS) — the element's `kill team hostile` is met, both bandits are shot
# down, and both vipers survive. That is a by-product; what the file is FOR is `flt_defer_s` on the
# SECOND shooter — the seconds it held its own trigger — together with `events.log`'s
# `flight COVER_DEFER` line and the cap it was holding against. `flt_both_s` is the same quantity from
# the other side: seconds in which the flight had nobody free.
# MEASURED: viper1 shoots at t=148.9 and is bound until t=162.0 (its AIM-120's time-to-active is
# 13.0 s from that range). viper2 reaches its own parameters inside that window, logs
# `COVER_DEFER ... capS=33.25` at t=154.4, holds for `flt_defer_s` = 7.8 s and fires at t=162.8 —
# 0.8 s after the window closed. `flt_both_s` is 0.0 for both: the flight was never uncovered.

unit viper1
  team friendly
  flight viper 1
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set pilot_shot_rtr 1.4
  set pilot_lock_nm 20
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit viper2
  team friendly
  flight viper 2
  module f16
  spawn 46.88334 6.40000 8150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set pilot_shot_rtr 1.4
  set pilot_lock_nm 20
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

# The two bandits fly straight and do not shoot: they are the geometry, not an opponent. The 0.04 deg
# of longitude between them (~3 km) is the stagger that separates the two firing solutions in TIME.
unit bandit1
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set rwr on
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450

unit bandit2
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.88334 7.89000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set rwr on
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
